winex11: Process captured mouse input independently of the window thread.

Force Commander can hold an application lock while polling DirectInput for
button release, with the window thread waiting for that lock. The X11 pointer
grab previously belonged to the window thread's connection, so the release
waited in its queue indefinitely. Native Windows delivers it independently.

Keep the clipping grab and its event pump on a lazy per-process input thread.
Retain core button events and existing XI2 motion handling, validate focus
before transferring the grab, drain pending caller input, and release any
implicit caller grab created during helper startup. Preserve desktop unmapping
and stop the helper's raw-motion subscription when capture is lost. Use an
event for the synchronous handoff so internal clipping cannot alter the
caller's message-queue wake masks or dispatch application messages.

The standalone dinput-capture-thread probe uses XTest input; SendInput tests
alone bypass the X connection responsible for this dependency.

